             ('Engineering judgment', 'Time and height both carry information.', '''<div class="decision-grid"><div class="decision"><h3>Observations versus target state</h3><p>A return describes what is observed now. A track represents continuity across observations. The illustration separates those two ideas so they can be inspected independently.</p></div><div class="decision"><h3>Height beyond a flat grid</h3><p>I worked on deployment issues involving height structure and overhanging obstacles, where a purely two-dimensional interpretation was insufficient.</p></div><div class="decision"><h3>Motion in context</h3><p>Supporting robot-motion information helps distinguish changes in observations from changes caused by the observing platform.</p></div><div class="decision"><h3>Extend an operating system</h3><p>The work was integration within an established framework: respecting existing interfaces and maintaining deployed behavior while adding capability.</p></div></div>'''),
